<h2>Where should the filters go on the account activity page?</h2>
<p class="subtitle">Rough wireframes, not final styling. All three filter in the browser, with no page reload. Click one to pick it.</p>

<style>
  .wf { font: 13px system-ui, sans-serif; border: 1px solid #ccd; border-radius: 6px; padding: 12px; background: #fff; color: #222; }
  .wf h4 { margin: 0 0 4px; font-size: 15px; }
  .wf .intro { margin: 0 0 10px; color: #666; font-size: 12px; }
  .wf .bar { display: flex; gap: 10px; align-items: flex-end; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-bottom: 8px; }
  .wf .field { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 3px; }
  .wf .field span { font-size: 11px; color: #555; }
  .wf .ctl { border: 1px solid #aab; border-radius: 4px; padding: 4px 8px; background: #fafbfc; min-width: 90px; }
  .wf .ctl.lg { min-width: 160px; }
  .wf .btn { border: 1px solid #889; border-radius: 4px; padding: 4px 10px; background: #eef; }
  .wf .tag { display: inline-block; border-radius: 10px; padding: 2px 8px; background: #dde6ff; margin-right: 6px; font-size: 12px; }
  .wf .count { font-size: 12px; color: #555; margin: 4px 0 6px; }
  .wf table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 11px; }
  .wf th { background: #f0f1f4; text-align: left; padding: 3px 5px; }
  .wf td { border-top: 1px solid #e3e5e8; padding: 3px 5px; }
  .wf .panel { border: 1px solid #889; border-radius: 6px; padding: 8px; background: #fbfbff; width: 210px; box-shadow: 0 2px 6px rgba(0,0,0,.15); margin: 0 0 8px auto; }
  .wf .panel div { margin-bottom: 6px; }
</style>

<div class="options">
  <div class="option" data-choice="a" onclick="toggleSelect(this)">
    <div class="letter">A</div>
    <div class="content">
      <h3>Inline filter bar</h3>
      <p>Every control is visible above the table. Changes apply as you make them. You can always see what is filtered.</p>
      <div class="wf">
        <h4>Account activity</h4>
        <p class="intro">Every sign-in and account change from the last 90 days, newest first.</p>
        <div class="bar">
          <label class="field"><span>Event type</span><div class="ctl">All events ▾</div></label>
          <label class="field"><span>Date range</span><div class="ctl">Last 90 days ▾</div></label>
          <label class="field"><span>Search device, location or IP</span><div class="ctl lg">🔍 &nbsp; ×</div></label>
        </div>
        <div class="count">Showing 48 of 48 events</div>
        <table><tr><th>When</th><th>Event</th><th>Device</th><th>Location</th><th>IP</th></tr>
          <tr><td>28 Sep, 19:42</td><td>Sign-in failed</td><td>Firefox, Windows</td><td>Unknown</td><td>203.0.113.x</td></tr></table>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="option" data-choice="b" onclick="toggleSelect(this)">
    <div class="letter">B</div>
    <div class="content">
      <h3>Inline bar plus active-filter tags</h3>
      <p>Same bar as A. Each active filter also shows as a removable tag, and there is a one-click "Failed sign-ins" shortcut, since that is what every support ticket was looking for.</p>
      <div class="wf">
        <h4>Account activity</h4>
        <p class="intro">Every sign-in and account change from the last 90 days, newest first.</p>
        <div class="bar">
          <label class="field"><span>Event type</span><div class="ctl">Sign-in failed ▾</div></label>
          <label class="field"><span>Date range</span><div class="ctl">Last 90 days ▾</div></label>
          <label class="field"><span>Search device, location or IP</span><div class="ctl lg">🔍 &nbsp; ×</div></label>
          <div class="btn">Show failed sign-ins</div>
        </div>
        <div><span class="tag">Sign-in failed ×</span></div>
        <div class="count">Showing 6 of 48 events</div>
        <table><tr><th>When</th><th>Event</th><th>Device</th><th>Location</th><th>IP</th></tr>
          <tr><td>28 Sep, 19:42</td><td>Sign-in failed</td><td>Firefox, Windows</td><td>Unknown</td><td>203.0.113.x</td></tr></table>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="option" data-choice="c" onclick="toggleSelect(this)">
    <div class="letter">C</div>
    <div class="content">
      <h3>"Filter" button with a panel</h3>
      <p>Keeps the page header quiet. Controls are hidden until you open the panel, so people may not notice filtering exists.</p>
      <div class="wf">
        <div class="bar" style="justify-content:space-between"><h4>Account activity</h4><div class="btn">Filter (1) ▾</div></div>
        <div class="panel">
          <div><span style="font-size:11px;color:#555">Event type</span><div class="ctl">Sign-in failed ▾</div></div>
          <div><span style="font-size:11px;color:#555">Date range</span><div class="ctl">Last 90 days ▾</div></div>
          <div><span style="font-size:11px;color:#555">Search</span><div class="ctl">🔍</div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="count">Showing 6 of 48 events</div>
        <table><tr><th>When</th><th>Event</th><th>Device</th><th>Location</th><th>IP</th></tr>
          <tr><td>28 Sep, 19:42</td><td>Sign-in failed</td><td>Firefox, Windows</td><td>Unknown</td><td>203.0.113.x</td></tr></table>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
